# PLACEHOLDER, and no longer something anyone has to remember to replace:
# packaging/build_release.sh overwrites this file in the staged payload with
# the public half of whatever --key signs that release, so a built release
# always carries the key matching its own signature. Editing this file by hand
# changes nothing about a real release.
#
# It survives only as the fallback for a source checkout that was never built
# by build_release.sh (services/updater.py reads it when no
# release_pubkey_file is configured). The matching private key is a throwaway
# and is not committed; see packaging/tests/. Keeping this in sync by hand is
# exactly what broke before: it matched only a gitignored local key, so the
# upgrade harness passed on one machine and failed in CI.
-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
MCowBQYDK2VwAyEAGZ/rStVno38RgOMWbVnHIRHHSk0WGVwhb4hMJnUkj/k=
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
